r them.”","verse":2},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"The LORD has done great things for us; we are filled with joy.","verse":3},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Restore our captives, O LORD, like streams in the Negev.","verse":4}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Zion","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":59,"href":"?bref=Ps.125.1-128.6","rawReference":"Ps.125.1-128.6"}],"ruleId":"Zion::Zion::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Zion"},"text":"A song of ascents. When the LORD restored the captives of Zion, we were like dreamers.","verse":1}],"id":"Zion","label":"Zion","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Zion::Zion::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Zion","term":"Zion"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Zion","sourceTitle":"Zion"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.120.1-134.3","r":"Ps.120.1-134.3","rawR":"Ps.120.1-134.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.120.1-134.3","value":"Ps.120.1-134.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 120–134"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These short, appealing songs were sung during pilgrims’ journeys to Jerusalem for the national festivals three times per year (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.16.16","r":"Deut.16.16","rawR":"Deut.16.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.16.16","value":"Deut.16.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deut 16:16"},"). The title of these psalms includes the Hebrew word for stairs, which some take to mean “ascending to Jerusalem.” These psalms (sometimes called the Songs of Ascents) take the reader on a pilgrimage to Jerusalem to praise God for his goodness to Israel throughout history."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.120.1-134.3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":134,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":120,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.120.1-134.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[120,121,122,123,124,125,126,127,128,129,130,131,132,133,134],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"804bdc0d4264fc96adf7bf16357af3c33f1b33647dde7b70863e764ccb4e0941","sourceItemName":"Ps.120.1-134.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7297,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.120.1-134.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.120.1-134.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.126.1-6","r":"Ps.126.1-6","rawR":"Ps.126.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.126.1-6","value":"Ps.126.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 126"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This hymn celebrates Israel’s return from exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.126.1-3","r":"Ps.126.1-3","rawR":"Ps.126.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.126.1-3","value":"Ps.126.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"126:1-3"},"). The psalmist prays for full restoration (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.126.4-6","r":"Ps.126.4-6","rawR":"Ps.126.4-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.126.4-6","value":"Ps.126.4-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"126:4-6"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.126.1-6","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":126,"endVerse":6,"startChapter":126,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.126.1-6","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[126],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a7b30e2f1988eacb217e47300b3fba98e708d7c8abd38abe508ff1ea5692d8a5","sourceItemName":"Ps.126.1-6","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7325,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.126.1-6","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.126.1-6","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.126.1-3","r":"Ps.126.1-3","rawR":"Ps.126.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.126.1-3","value":"Ps.126.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"126:1-3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The Lord brought about Israel’s restoration from exile, just as he had brought Israel out of Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.1","r":"Ps.114.1","rawR":"Ps.114.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.1","value":"Ps.114.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"114:1"},"). The restoration transformed the weeping of the Lord’s people into ",{"c":["laughter"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and showed the Lord’s character to the ",{"c":["nations"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.9.11","r":"Ps.9.11","rawR":"Ps.9.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.9.11","value":"Ps.9.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.64.9","r":"Ps.64.9","rawR":"Ps.64.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.64.9","value":"Ps.64.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"64:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.12.4","r":"Isa.12.4","rawR":"Isa.12.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.12.4","value":"Isa.12.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 12:4"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.126.1-3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":126,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":126,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.126.1-3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[126],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"939e0b41e509f0f4ab06e1c3b6231d1e921862405e32fb1bcf7707237c898246","sourceItemName":"Ps.126.1-3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7326,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.126.1-3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.126.1-3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.126.4-6","r":"Ps.126.4-6","rawR":"Ps.126.4-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.126.4-6","value":"Ps.126.4-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"126:4-6"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The prophets had spoken of the restoration as a time when the wilderness would change into the Garden of Eden (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.51.3","r":"Isa.51.3","rawR":"Isa.51.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.51.3","value":"Isa.51.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 51:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.47.1-23","r":"Ezek.47.1-23","rawR":"Ezek.47.1-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.47.1-23","value":"Ezek.47.1-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezek 47"},"); the reality fell far short of paradise. Here the restoration community prays for full redemption (see ",{"href":"?bref=Hagg.2.19","r":"Hagg.2.19","rawR":"Hagg.2.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hagg.2.19","value":"Hagg.2.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hag 2:19"},"). • ",{"c":["as streams renew the desert:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The seasonal rains filled the dry river beds (",{"c":["wadis"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"},"), and the land turned green again. The prayer looks for a similar transformation of Israel’s ",{"c":["fortunes"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," a fulfillment of the imagery of the “Second Exodus” in Isaiah (see “",{"href":"?item=ThePromiseOfASecondExodus_ThemeNote_Filament","id":"ThePromiseOfASecondExodus_ThemeNote_Filament","rawId":"ThePromiseOfASecondExodus_ThemeNote_Filament","t":"link","v":"The Promise of a Second Exodus"},"” Theme Note). • The ",{"c":["harvest"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," represents God’s full restoration."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.126.4-6","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":126,"endVerse":6,"startChapter":126,"startVerse":4}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.126.4-6","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[126],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b4afa86adec70b4fca0565ab597715bbcfe9d245a44ba04c3568810b724150d5","sourceItemName":"Ps.126.4-6","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7327,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.126.4-6","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.126.4-6","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}